t;\\u003e Roblox:\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eLike Material Generator, you should not give prompts designed to create content pertaining to existing intellectual property for which you don’t have the rights.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003c/aside\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eWhere is the system that alerts you of IP infringement before bans? Roblox has yet to impliment something that isn’t immediate termination, and enforces this on decades-old assets. You’re expecting the honor system to play out right. we all know thats not the case. what are the prevention steps for infringement issues that aren’t “hey guys be kind and follow the law.” I ask this because corporate has quite literally told me my own work wasn’t stolen when doing DMCA requests for entirely stolen games. Roblox as a company themselves falls flat on IP infringement, and this seems like a cheap way to push fault for something that should have stronger safeguards.\\u003c/p\\u003e\&quot;,\&quot;post_number\&quot;:15,\&quot;post_type\&quot;:1,\&quot;posts_count\&quot;:52,\&quot;updated_at\&quot;:\&quot;2024-03-20T17:02:44.191Z\&quot;,\&quot;reply_count\&quot;:0,\&quot;reply_to_post_number\&quot;:null,\&quot;quote_count\&quot;:1,\&quot;incoming_link_count\&quot;:4,\&quot;reads\&quot;:525,\&quot;readers_count\&quot;:524,\&quot;score\&quot;:170.0,\&quot;yours\&quot;:false,\&quot;topic_id\&quot;:2881851,\&quot;topic_slug\&quot;:\&quot;protecting-intellectual-property-when-using-generative-ai\&quot;,\&quot;display_username\&quot;:\&quot;aech\&quot;,\&quot;primary_group_name\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_name\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_url\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_bg_color\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_color\&quot;:null,\&quot;flair_group_id\&quot;:null,\&quot;badges_granted\&quot;:[],\&quot;version\&quot;:4,\&quot;can_edit\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_delete\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_recover\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_see_hidden_post\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_wiki\&quot;:false,\&quot;read\&quot;:true,\&quot;user_title\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;bookmarked\&quot;:false,\&quot;actions_summary\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:2,\&quot;count\&quot;:3}],\&quot;moderator\&quot;:false,\&quot;admin\&quot;:false,\&quot;staff\&quot;:false,\&quot;user_id\&quot;:46290,\&quot;hidden\&quot;:false,\&quot;trust_level\&quot;:1,\&quot;deleted_at\&quot;:null,\&quot;user_deleted\&quot;:false,\&quot;edit_reason\&quot;:null,\&quot;can_view_edit_history\&quot;:false,\&quot;wiki\&quot;:false,\&quot;post_url\&quot;:\&quot;/t/protecting-intellectual-property-when-using-generative-ai/2881851/15\&quot;,\&quot;can_accept_answer\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_unaccept_answer\&quot;:false,\&quot;accepted_answer\&quot;:false,\&quot;topic_accepted_answer\&quot;:false,\&quot;can_translate\&quot;:false,\&quot;is_translated\&quot;:false,\&quot;detected_language\&quot;:null},{\&quot;id\&quot;:10506077,\&quot;name\&quot;:\&quot;checkersoda\&quot;,\&quot;username\&quot;:\&quot;checkersoda\&quot;,\&quot;avatar_template\&quot;:\&quot;/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/checkersoda/{size}/6994274_2.png\&quot;,\&quot;created_at\&quot;:\&quot;2024-03-20T18:33:59.433Z\&quot;,\&quot;cooked\&quot;:\&quot;\\u003cp\\u003eIn the \\u003ca href=\\\&quot;https://devforum.roblox.com/t/texture-generator-beta/2880635\\\&quot;\\u003eTexture Generator post\\u003c/a\\u003e, it’s specified that:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cblockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eThe Texture Generator is trained using \\u003cstrong\\u003ethird-party\\u003c/strong\\u003e and in-house models on \\u003cstrong\\u003epublicly available data\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003c/blockquote\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eWhat exactly is the ‘third-party’ model and ‘publicly available data’ here?\\u003c/strong\\u003e One could make the argument that the ‘third-party’ model(s) is the same as other models that scrape from artists’ works. ‘Publicly available data’ can just be a professional term for Google Images.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n